@startuml j1-first-visit-and-ask
!include c4-sequence.iuml
title J1 First visit and ask
actor "Patient" as Patient <<person>>
box "In the patient's browser"
participant "Patient chat\n(chat.js, sync.js,\nshared.js)" as Chat <<container>>
participant "Rules engine\n(core.js)" as Core <<component>>
database "Browser storage\n(localStorage)" as LS <<store>>
end box
box "Vercel functions"
participant "api/clinic.js\napi/messages.js\napi/tickets.js" as R <<container>>
participant "api/chat.js" as Api <<container>>
end box
participant "OpenRouter" as OR <<external>>
database "Postgres\n(Neon)" as Store <<store>>

== Opening the chat ==
Patient -> Chat : opens the live link
Chat -> R : shared.js: GET /api/clinic
R -> Store : read the saved clinic file
R --> Chat : the saved file, or the\nshipped clinic-data.json
Chat --> Patient : the welcome line and\nseven quick replies
== A question ==
Patient -> Chat : taps "Timings", or\ntypes a question\nand presses Send
Chat -> R : shared.js: POST /api/messages\n(the question, with\nthis browser's key)
R -> Store : a row in the\ntable messages
Chat -> Core : FD.answer(question,\nclinic file, language)
Core --> Chat : the draft answer and\nthe facts it holds
note over Core, R : The rules engine always answers first;\nthe model may only reword the draft.
Chat -> Api : POST /api/chat (the draft,\nits facts, the language,\nthe clinic file)
alt the model answers in time and passes the guard
  Api -> OR : reword the draft;\nthe patient's message\nis not sent
  OR --> Api : the reworded text
  Api -> Api : FD.guard checks the\ntext against the draft\nand the file
  Api --> Chat : 200 with the checked text
  Chat -> Core : FD.guard checks it\nagain in the browser
else no answer in time, or a check fails
  note over Chat, Api : the draft is shown as it is (see J9)
end
Chat -> Core : FD.addTicket (question,\nreply, status "answered")
Core -> LS : the ticket joins\nthis browser's tickets
Chat --> Patient : the answer, with\n"Listen", "Helpful"\nand "Not helpful"
Chat -> R : shared.js: POST /api/messages\n(the reply)
R -> Store : a second row in\nthe table messages
Chat -> R : sync.js: POST /api/tickets\n(the ticket, with\nthis browser's key)
R -> Store : a row in the table\ntickets, owned by\nthe hash of the key
note left of Store : tickets and messages\nare deleted after 7 days
@enduml
